00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:48.160
The crew moves on to the tranquil English countryside. Here, they will explore the origins

00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:55.040
of powered flight itself. This is the domain of the dragonfly.

00:14:55.040 --> 00:15:01.640
We are at Wiccan Fren in Cambridge. It's particularly important for us because it has no less than

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:08.040
23 different species of dragonfly on it, which is what we've come to see.

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:14.840
Filming a scene with David introducing the dragonfly as essentially our most primitive

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:20.800
insect flyer. So this is the first form of flight that's been discovered on the planet.

00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:27.920
We're hoping to get some shots from our boat, some dragonflies flitting around. Then I think

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:30.320
it should look spectacular.

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:36.320
It's taken days to capture the right dragonflies, and now they must perform for the camera.

